---
export const title = 'Moving cards';
export const order = 200;
import DemoComponentCard from '../../../../components/DemoComponentCard.astro';
---

<p>
  With a mouse or pen, drag a card; on touch, hold it for a moment first, so a swipe still scrolls.
  A placeholder shows where it will land, and the board and the column scroll when the card nears
  their edges. <kbd>Escape</kbd> cancels the drag. Buttons and links inside a card keep their own
  clicks and do not start a drag.
</p>
<p>
  Dropping a card in a new place fires the cancelable <code>card-move</code> event with
  <code>{'{'} cardId, fromColumn, toColumn, fromIndex, toIndex {'}'}</code> (0-based,
  <code>toIndex</code> is the card's index in <code>toColumn</code> after the move). Unless you
  cancel it, the board applies the move and replaces <code>cards</code> with a new array, the moved
  card a copy with its new <code>columnId</code>. To confirm a move with a server first, cancel
  the event and apply it once the server agrees with <code>applyKanbanMove(cards, detail)</code>,
  exported with the component.
</p>

<DemoComponentCard lang={'html'}>
  <wc-kanban id='kanban-cancel' label='Approvals' style='width: 100%; height: 20rem;'></wc-kanban>
  <script is:inline>
    const $approvals = document.getElementById('kanban-cancel');
    $approvals.columns = [
      { id: 'new', title: 'New' },
      { id: 'approved', title: 'Approved' },
      { id: 'locked', title: 'Locked' },
    ];
    $approvals.cards = [
      { id: 'a', columnId: 'new', title: 'Expense report' },
      { id: 'b', columnId: 'new', title: 'Travel request' },
      { id: 'c', columnId: 'locked', title: 'Audit (cannot move)' },
    ];
    $approvals.addEventListener('card-move', event => {
      const { cardId, toColumn } = event.detail;
      if (cardId === 'c' || toColumn === 'locked') {
        event.preventDefault();
        myConsole.log('card-move canceled');
      }
    });
  </script>
</DemoComponentCard>
